1","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo>≥</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>258</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>241</mn></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"mombh_verified_ne_solved","name":"3 measured, 1 simplistic model, 0 solved — and 3 sits below the stellar ceiling 30.","why":"3 measured, 1 simplistic model, 0 solved — and 3 sits below the stellar ceiling 30.","statement":"(3 >= 1) ∧ (0 < 1) ∧ (30 > 3)","address":"51fd525f-cda7-8b34-930a-9498dc4c0cf3","skill":"paper-trial","tex":"3 \\ge 1 \\quad\\land\\quad 0 < 1 \\quad\\land\\quad 30 > 3","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>30</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"mombh_quantum_balmer_edge_is_rydberg_quarter","name":"QUANTUM: E(n=2→∞) = 13.6/4 = 3.4 eV (×10: 136/4 = 34); λ = 12398/3.4 = 3646 Å (12398/34 = 364, ×10). The break sits at the n=2 ionisation edge.","why":"QUANTUM: E(n=2→∞) = 13.6/4 = 3.4 eV (×10: 136/4 = 34); λ = 12398/3.4 = 3646 Å (12398/34 = 364, ×10). The break sits at the n=2 ionisation edge.","statement":"(136 / 4 = 34) ∧ (12398 / 34 = 364)","address":"09840495-60a9-8c72-aad6-db200aa910d1","skill":"paper-trial","tex":"\\frac{136}{4} = 34 \\quad\\land\\quad \\left\\lfloor \\frac{12398}{34} \\right\\rfloor = 364","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>136</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>34</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\">&#x230A;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>12398</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>34</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"true\">&#x230B;</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>364</mn></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":{"kind":"predict-the-value","at":31,"length":3}},{"key":"mombh_variability_is_four_sigma","name":"30 ± 7 %: 4·7 ≤ 30 < 5·7. SCOPE: three instruments.","why":"30 ± 7 %: 4·7 ≤ 30 < 5·7. SCOPE: three instruments.","statement":"(4 * 7 <= 30) ∧ (30 < 5 * 7)","address":"15441eaa-2039-8fe6-9687-ca98c63fb7b3","skill":"paper-trial","tex":"4 \\cdot 7 \\le 30 \\quad\\land\\quad 30 < 5 \\cdot 7","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>30</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"mombh_hbeta_oiii_ratio_central_over_ten_lower_under","name":"11.4 (−2.5) ×10: central clears 10, lower bound does not.","why":"11.4 (−2.5) ×10: central clears 10, lower bound does not.","statement":"(114 > 100) ∧ (114 - 25 = 89) ∧ (89 < 100)","address":"eb0a362d-57c1-8408-b992-3a3d9de290c0","skill":"paper-trial","tex":"114 > 100 \\quad\\land\\quad 114 - 25 = 89 \\quad\\land\\quad 89 < 100","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>114</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>114</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>89</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>89</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":{"kind":"predict-the-value","at":26,"length":2}},{"key":"mombh_balmer_break_exceeds_stellar_ceiling","name":"Break 7.7 (−1.4) lower bound 6.3 > A-star ceiling 5 > Chabrier ceiling 3 (×10). SCOPE: ceilings are model inputs.","why":"Break 7.7 (−1.4) lower bound 6.3 > A-star ceiling 5 > Chabrier ceiling 3 (×10). SCOPE: ceilings are model inputs.","statement":"(77 - 14 = 63) ∧ (63 > 